<title>INDIA: Indian soybean markets closed for second day.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean markets closed for second day.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean markets were closed for the second day on Tuesday for a local religious festival, dealers said.</p>
<p>They were closed on Monday for the Ganesh festival. The markets reopen on Wednesday.</p>
<p>On the last trading day on Friday, prices were steady on low volumes.</p>
